# Description
This PR introduces the bless LLM extension integration for the browser-runtime.
A simple example is provided (JS) which displays how one can utilize the host runtime(s) LLM plugin.

The build-step has been updated to compile the JS file to wasm - utilizing bless network's [javy plugins](https://github.com/blessnetwork/javy-bless-plugins).

## Example usage of the LLM extension/plugin from JS
```javascript
// Create instance
const llm = BlessLLM("Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct-q4f32_1-MLC");

// Set options
llm.setOptions({
    system_message: "You are a helpful assistant. First time I ask, your name will be Lucy. Second time I ask, your name will be Bob."
});

// Chat
console.log(llm.chat("What is your name?"));
console.log(llm.chat("What is your name?"));
```

